requirements
C1 18 supported CircuitBreaker is a state machine that prevents sending requests likely to fail.
C2 19 unclear NewCircuitBreaker creates a new CircuitBreaker from Settings.
C3 41 supported MaxRequests bounds how many requests may pass through in half-open state.
C4 43 supported If MaxRequests is 0, only 1 request is allowed in half-open state.
C5 45 supported Interval defines the cyclic period of the closed state for clearing internal Counts.
C6 47 supported If Interval is 0, internal Counts are not cleared during the closed state.
C7 49 supported Timeout is the period of the open state after which the state becomes half-open.
C8 51 supported If Timeout is 0, its value is set to 60 seconds.
C9 53 supported ReadyToTrip is called with a copy of Counts whenever a request fails in the closed state.
C10 54 supported If ReadyToTrip returns true, CircuitBreaker is placed into the open state.
C11 55 supported If ReadyToTrip is nil, a default ReadyToTrip is used.
C12 56 supported Default ReadyToTrip returns true when consecutive failures exceed 5.
C13 58 supported OnStateChange is called whenever CircuitBreaker's state changes.
C14 60 supported IsSuccessful is called with the error returned from a request.
C15 61 supported If IsSuccessful returns true, the error counts as a success.
C16 62 supported Otherwise the error counts as a failure.
C17 63 supported If IsSuccessful is nil, a default is used that returns false for all non-nil errors.
C18 77 supported CircuitBreaker clears internal Counts on state change or at closed-state intervals.
C19 78 supported Counts on the change of state or at closed-state intervals; Counts ignores results of requests sent before clearing.
C20 79 supported Counts ignores results of requests sent before clearing.
C21 87 supported Execute runs the given request if CircuitBreaker accepts it.
C22 88 supported Execute returns an error instantly if CircuitBreaker rejects the request.
C23 89 supported Otherwise Execute returns the result of the request.
C24 90 supported If a panic occurs in the request, CircuitBreaker handles it as an error and causes the same panic again.
source
C1 16 supported The CircuitBreaker has three states: closed, half-open, and open.
C2 23 None ErrTooManyRequests is returned when the breaker is half open and the request count is over maxRequests.
C3 25 supported ErrOpenState is returned when the breaker is open.
C4 48 unclear Counts includes Requests, TotalSuccesses, TotalFailures, ConsecutiveSuccesses, and ConsecutiveFailures.
C5 44 supported The internal Counts are cleared on a change of state or at the closed-state intervals.
C6 46 supported Counts ignores results of requests sent before clearing.
C7 56 supported onRequest increments Requests.
C8 60 unclear onSuccess increments TotalSuccesses and ConsecutiveSuccesses and resets ConsecutiveFailures to zero.
C9 66 unclear onFailure increments TotalFailures and ConsecutiveFailures and resets ConsecutiveSuccesses to zero.
C10 72 unclear clear resets all five counters to zero.
C11 83 supported MaxRequests is the maximum number of requests allowed to pass through when the breaker is half-open.
C12 85 supported If MaxRequests is 0, the breaker allows only 1 request.
C13 87 supported Interval is the cyclic period of the closed state for clearing the internal Counts.
C14 89 supported If Interval is less than or equal to 0, Counts are not cleared during the closed state.
C15 91 supported Timeout is the period of the open state, after which the state becomes half-open.
C16 93 supported If Timeout is less than or equal to 0, the timeout value is set to 60 seconds.
C17 95 supported ReadyToTrip is called with a copy of Counts whenever a request fails in the closed state.
C18 96 supported If ReadyToTrip returns true, the breaker is placed into the open state.
C19 98 supported The default ReadyToTrip returns true when the number of consecutive failures is more than 5.
C20 100 supported OnStateChange is called whenever the state changes.
C21 102 supported IsSuccessful is called with the error returned from a request; if it returns true, the error is counted as a success, otherwise as a failure.
C22 105 supported The default IsSuccessful returns false for all non-nil errors.
C23 147 supported NewCircuitBreaker sets maxRequests to 1 when Settings.MaxRequests is 0, otherwise uses the given value.
C24 153 supported NewCircuitBreaker sets interval to defaultInterval when Settings.Interval <= 0.
C25 159 supported NewCircuitBreaker sets timeout to defaultTimeout when Settings.Timeout <= 0.
C26 165 supported NewCircuitBreaker uses defaultReadyToTrip when Settings.ReadyToTrip is nil.
C27 171 supported NewCircuitBreaker uses defaultIsSuccessful when Settings.IsSuccessful is nil.
C28 177 supported NewCircuitBreaker calls toNewGeneration at construction time.
C29 189 supported defaultInterval is zero seconds and defaultTimeout is 60 seconds.
C30 190 supported defaultTimeout is 60 seconds.
C31 193 supported defaultReadyToTrip returns true when ConsecutiveFailures > 5.
C32 197 supported defaultIsSuccessful returns true only when err is nil.
C33 211 supported State() acquires the mutex, calls currentState, and returns the resulting state.
C34 220 supported Counts() acquires the mutex and returns the internal counts.
C35 224 supported Execute returns an error instantly if the breaker rejects the request.
C36 226 supported If a panic occurs in the request, Execute handles it as an error and causes the same panic again.
C37 229 supported Execute calls beforeRequest and returns its error without running the request if error occurs.
C38 237 supported Execute's deferred recover records the panic as a failure via afterRequest(false) and re-panics.
C39 243 supported Execute records the request outcome via afterRequest using isSuccessful(err).
C40 262 supported TwoStepCircuitBreaker.Allow checks whether a request can proceed and returns a callback for reporting success or failure separately.
C41 266 supported Allow calls beforeRequest and returns its error if not allowed.
C42 272 supported The callback returned by Allow calls afterRequest with the recorded generation and the boolean success value.
C43 283 supported beforeRequest acquires the mutex, calls currentState, and rejects with ErrOpenState when the state is open.
C44 285 supported beforeRequest rejects with ErrTooManyRequests when state is half-open and Requests >= maxRequests.
C45 289 supported beforeRequest increments Requests via onRequest when the request is accepted.
C46 299 supported afterRequest ignores the outcome if the current generation differs from the generation captured before the request.
C47 303 supported afterRequest dispatches to onSuccess or onFailure based on the success flag.
C48 313 supported In closed state, onSuccess calls counts.onSuccess.
C49 316 supported In half-open state, onSuccess calls counts.onSuccess and transitions to closed when ConsecutiveSuccesses >= maxRequests.
C50 326 supported In closed state, onFailure calls counts.onFailure and transitions to open when readyToTrip returns true.
C51 330 supported In half-open state, onFailure transitions to open.
C52 337 supported currentState in closed state calls toNewGeneration when expiry is nonzero and has passed.
C53 341 supported currentState in open state transitions to half-open when expiry has passed.
C54 345 supported currentState returns the current state and generation.
C55 349 supported setState returns without change if the target state equals the current state.
C56 353 supported setState records the previous state, assigns the new state, and calls toNewGeneration.
C57 358 supported setState calls onStateChange with name, previous state, and new state if the callback is non-nil.
C58 364 supported toNewGeneration increments the generation and clears counts.
C59 370 supported In toNewGeneration for closed state, expiry is zero when interval is 0, otherwise now+interval.
C60 376 supported In toNewGeneration for open state, expiry is now+timeout.
C61 378 supported In toNewGeneration for half-open state (default), expiry is zero.
C62 242 unclear Execute acquires a generation via beforeRequest before invoking req, and then calls afterRequest with that generation.
C63 238 supported On Execute, a panic in req triggers the deferred recover to call afterRequest(false) before re-panicking.
C64 271 supported On Allow, beforeRequest runs first and the returned callback later calls afterRequest.
C65 356 supported In setState, generation update and counts clearing via toNewGeneration occur before onStateChange is invoked.
C66 369 supported In new-generation processing for closed state, the interval is checked before expiry is set or zeroed.
tests
C1 116 supported State constants are State(0)=StateClosed, State(1)=StateHalfOpen, State(2)=StateOpen.
C2 120 supported StateClosed, StateHalfOpen, and StateOpen have string forms "closed", "half-open", and "open" respectively.
C3 123 supported An unknown state value 100 formats as "unknown state: 100".
C4 131 unclear A default CircuitBreaker constructed with empty Settings has name "", maxRequests 1, interval 0, timeout 60s, StateClosed state, zero counts, and zero expiry.
C5 132 unclear A default CircuitBreaker has a non-nil readyToTrip and a nil onStateChange.
C6 140 unclear A CircuitBreaker built with custom settings reflects name "cb", maxRequests 3, interval 30s, timeout 90s, non-nil readyToTrip and onStateChange, StateClosed, zero counts, and non-zero expiry.
C7 152 unclear Negative Interval and Timeout settings are normalized to interval 0 and timeout 60s, with a nil onStateChange and zero expiry.
C8 168 supported With default settings, five failures leave the breaker in StateClosed with counts {5, 0, 5, 0, 5}.
C9 172 supported A success while in StateClosed updates counts to {6, 1, 5, 1, 0}.
C10 182 None After a total of 6 consecutive failures the default breaker transitions from StateClosed to StateOpen, with counts reset to zero and a non-zero expiry.
C11 186 supported While StateOpen, both succeed and fail return errors, and counts remain zero.
C12 195 supported After pseudoSleeping 59s while StateOpen the breaker remains StateOpen; after 1 more second (over Timeout) it becomes StateHalfOpen with zero expiry.
C13 199 unclear A failure while StateHalfOpen transitions the breaker to StateOpen with counts reset to zero and non-zero expiry.
C14 211 unclear A success in StateHalfOpen transitions the default breaker to StateClosed with zero counts and zero expiry.
C15 239 unclear With custom settings, alternating successes and failures keep the breaker StateClosed until the custom ReadyToTrip (requests >= 3 and failure ratio >= 0.6) trips.
C16 242 supported A successful state change invokes OnStateChange with the breaker name and from/to states.
C17 248 supported After pseudoSleeping 90s (Timeout) with custom settings, the breaker goes StateOpen to StateHalfOpen and OnStateChange fires with {Open, HalfOpen}.
C18 259 supported In StateHalfOpen with maxRequests 3, a third in-flight request is counted before completion, and an additional request over MaxRequests returns an error.
C19 264 supported After the third consecutive success in StateHalfOpen completes, the breaker transitions to StateClosed with zero counts and fires OnStateChange {HalfOpen, Closed}.
C20 276 unclear The TwoStepCircuitBreaker mirrors the single-step breaker's counts and state transitions.
C21 326 supported A panic in the request propagates to the caller and is counted as a failure with counts {1, 0, 1, 0, 1}.
C22 341 unclear A request from a previous generation does not affect the current generation's counts after Interval elapses.
C23 355 supported A custom IsSuccessful function can reclassify failures as successes, updating TotalSuccesses and ConsecutiveSuccesses.
C24 365 supported After replacing isSuccessful with nil-checking, 6 failures under the new rule trip the breaker to StateOpen.
C25 391 contradicted Concurrent successes across 10 goroutines totaling 100000 requests all return nil and produce counts {total, total, 0, total, 0}.
